- entry .Traversable   re-exported from `murmuration`: the typeclass of anything which can be traversed element by element
-     `import rudiments.*` presents the collection typeclasses as one surface, so `Traversable`,
-     `Reshapable`, `Mappable`, `Reversible`, `Inclusive`, `Convertible`, `Keyed`,
-     `Intersectable`, `Iterator` and `SortAlgorithm`, with the operations written over them,
-     are exported here from `murmuration`. Each has its full account on its `murmuration` page;
-     the operations which need `Ordinal` or `Optional` (`each`, `seek`, `where`, `head`, …) are
-     declared in `rudiments` itself.
- entry .Reshapable   re-exported from `murmuration`: rebuilds a collection in its own shape from transformed elements
- entry .Mappable   re-exported from `murmuration`: the value-mapping typeclass behind `map`
- entry .Reversible   re-exported from `murmuration`: the typeclass behind `reverse`
- entry .Inclusive   re-exported from `murmuration`: the membership typeclass behind `has`
- entry .Convertible   re-exported from `murmuration`: conversion to a requested shape, behind `to[Form]`
- entry .Keyed   re-exported from `murmuration`: a container with keys and values, behind `keys` and `values`
- entry .Intersectable   re-exported from `murmuration`: the set-algebra typeclass behind `intersect` and `except`
- entry .SortAlgorithm   re-exported from `murmuration`: a sorting algorithm, chosen from `sortingAlgorithms`
- entry .Iterator   re-exported from `murmuration`: the one-shot traversal whose `next()` yields `Iterator.Exhausted` at the end
- entry .reverse   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements in reverse order
- entry .has   re-exported from `murmuration`: whether a collection contains a value (a `Map` its key)
- entry .map   re-exported from `murmuration`: transforms each element (a `Map`'s values), shape-preservingly
- entry .remap   re-exported from `murmuration`: transforms each element (a `Map`'s pairs) into a new shape
- entry .bind   re-exported from `murmuration`: the monadic bind, each element to a collection, flattened
- entry .flatMap   re-exported from `murmuration`: `bind` under the name `for`-comprehensions desugar to
- entry .filter   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements satisfying a predicate; there is no `filterNot`
- entry .withFilter   re-exported from `murmuration`: the guard a `for`-comprehension desugars to
- entry .foreach   re-exported from `murmuration`: visits each element; `each` is the preferred spelling
- entry .exists   re-exported from `murmuration`: whether some element satisfies a predicate
- entry .fold   re-exported from `murmuration`: a left fold with a two-parameter lambda; `fuse` is the contextual form
- entry .flat   re-exported from `murmuration`: flattens one level of nesting
- entry .trace   re-exported from `murmuration`: a left fold keeping every intermediate state
- entry .excerpt   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements between two zero-based positions
- entry .group   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements grouped by a key into a `Map`
- entry .distinct   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements with duplicates removed
- entry .deduplicate   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements with duplicates by a key removed
- entry .zip   re-exported from `murmuration`: pairs the elements of two collections
- entry .batched   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements in groups of a size
- entry .span   re-exported from `murmuration`: splits at the first element failing a predicate
- entry .partition   re-exported from `murmuration`: splits into the elements satisfying a predicate and the rest
- entry .sweep   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements a partial function accepts, transformed; the stdlib's `collect`
- entry .keys   re-exported from `murmuration`: the keys of a keyed container
- entry .values   re-exported from `murmuration`: the values of a keyed container
- entry .count   re-exported from `murmuration`: how many elements satisfy a predicate; `count(_ == x)` counts a value
- entry .intersect   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements two sets share
- entry .except   re-exported from `murmuration`: the elements of a set not in another
