-   entry .apply   `Scroll[element](capacity)` makes an empty scroll; `scroll(index)` reads an element
-       Two overloads which share the name. On the companion, `Scroll[element](capacity)` makes
-       an empty scroll with at least 16 slots, and needs a `ClassTag` for the element. As an
-       extension on a scroll, `scroll(index)` is the element at a zero-based `Int`, checked
-       against the length, throwing `IndexOutOfBoundsException` beyond it.
