-   entry .isEmpty   `scroll.isEmpty`: whether a scroll holds no elements
-   entry .update   `scroll(index) = value`: replaces the element of a scroll at an index below its length
-   entry .last   `scroll.last`: the most recently appended element of a scroll; throws on an empty one
-   entry .append   appends to a scroll one element, every element of another scroll, or a window of a JVM array
-   entry .retract   `scroll.retract(count)`: forgets a scroll's last `count` elements, keeping the capacity
-   entry .clear   `scroll.clear()`: forgets every element of a scroll, keeping the capacity
-   entry .freeze   `scroll.freeze`: the elements so far, as an exact-size frozen array; the scroll is unchanged
